WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.280
Rescuers search for thousands missing in Nepal's floods as aid cuts raise risks for millions in the Himalayas. This is Omni View, episode 184. Rescue teens in Nepal are still looking for thousands of people reported missing after flash floods struck in August. Funding reductions have cut support for climate monitoring and research programs across the Himalayan region. Officials note that these reductions leave more communities exposed to future extreme weather.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:34.000
The search operations continue in remote areas where access remains difficult due to damage

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.780
droids and ongoing weather concerns. Aid organizations have reported that the scale of missing

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:45.580
persons has strained local resources beyond initial estimates. The Associated Press reports

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:51.220
ongoing searches tied directly to the August floods and links the aid reductions to broader cuts

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:57.300
in programs previously supported by the United States. Reuters coverage of regional weather risks

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:02.380
emphasizes how monitoring gaps affect early warning systems used by governments in Nepal,

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:08.280
India, and China. Both accounts describe the same sequence of flooding followed by reduced

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:14.900
external support, yet they differ in focus, one centers on immediate human recovery while the other

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:20.480
highlights long-term data collection for hazard prediction. The reporting shows that the cuts have

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:25.740
affected stations that previously tracked river levels and rainfall patterns across multiple countries

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.040
sharing the mountain range.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:32.540
Local authorities in Nepal have coordinated with international teams to prioritize areas

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:35.060
with the highest number of reported disappearances.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:40.640
The search continues in difficult terrain while the data gaps widen exposure for communities

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.040
that rely on those same monitoring tools.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:48.300
Russian forces have increased use of long-range weapons against targets inside Ukraine.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:54.480
The Economist reports this shift adds physical, psychological, and economic strain on Ukrainian

00:01:54.480 --> 00:02:00.040
and civilian areas. No immediate change in battlefield lines has been recorded.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:05.460
The strikes have targeted infrastructure that supports daily operations across multiple regions.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:09.620
Ukrainian responses have focused on maintaining defensive positions

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:12.140
while managing the added pressure on supply routes.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:16.980
The economist frames the capability increase as part of a sustained campaign

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:20.460
that limits Ukrainian options for rest or resupply.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:25.280
Ukraine. Ukrainian officials have described the strikes as attempts to erode public support

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:30.760
for continued resistance. Both descriptions rest on the same observed pattern of repeated

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:36.200
long-range attacks without claiming a decisive territorial shift. The coverage notes that

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:41.100
the new weapon systems allow strikes from greater distances than earlier phases of the conflict.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:46.200
International observers have tracked the frequency of these attacks through open-source data

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:51.660
on impact sites. The strikes continue without altering front lines while the added reach

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:57.460
increases pressure on Ukrainian logistics. US President Donald Trump held his first meeting

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:03.060
with UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham. Trump stated he could work with the new Prime Minister while

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:09.200
describing the Chagos Islands agreement as problematic. The discussion covered bilateral cooperation on

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:15.040
security matters alongside the specific policy disagreement. UK officials have maintained that

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.780
that the agreement supports broader regional stability goals.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:23.160
BBC reporting presents the meeting as an early diplomatic contact between the two leaders

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:27.980
that included both cooperation signals and explicit criticism of one policy.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:33.860
UK government statements have defended the Chagos arrangement as necessary for regional security

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:34.380
arrangements.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:39.060
The accounts agree on the occurrence of the meeting and the public mention of the Chagos

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:39.420
issue.

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:44.580
They differ on whether the criticism signals a broader shift in US-UK coordination.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:49.460
The exchange occurred during scheduled talks in New York ahead of larger international

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:50.000
gatherings.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:54.780
Both sides described the overall tone as constructive despite the noted difference.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:04:00.140
The leaders addressed shared security topics while the Chagos point remained a clear point

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:00.760
of divergence.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:06.620
An Indian court ruled that goods sold in duty-free shops remained subject to national laws.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:12.600
The decision affects sales of nicotine pouches by the Adani Group at airports, which authorities

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:15.460
Studies classify as illegal under domestic drug rules.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:21.020
The ruling clarifies that airport retail zones do not operate outside standard enforcement

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:21.620
mechanisms.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:27.260
The Adani Group had argued for exemption based on the international status of the facilities.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:33.040
Reuters notes the ruling rejects arguments that duty-free zones operate outside ordinary

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:34.240
Indian regulations.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:39.360
The Adani Group had sought exemption on the basis of international airport status.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:43.160
Both sides accept that the products were sold at airport outlets.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:48.400
The disagreement centers on whether those outlets fall under standard national enforcement.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:54.040
The court decision follows earlier regulatory actions by New Delhi against the same items.

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:59.420
Legal representatives for the company have indicated plans to review the judgment for possible

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:00.260
further steps.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:05.980
The ruling keeps duty-free sales inside the same legal framework that applies elsewhere in

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:06.380
the country.

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:12.260
The head of the Inter-American Development Bank is preparing a possible $2.5 billion

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:14.060
loan package for Venezuela.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.360
Board members have raised objections to the proposal.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:21.700
The financing would target economic stabilization measures if approved.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:27.360
Venezuelan officials have expressed interest in the funds for immediate use in public services.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:33.480
Reuters reports the effort continues despite internal resistance over lending terms and oversight.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:38.540
Right. Venezuelan authorities have welcomed the potential funds for economic stabilization.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:43.980
The reporting agrees on the loan size under discussion and the existence of board concerns.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:48.800
The proposal has moved forward through preliminary internal reviews at the bank.

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:53.600
Discussions continue on conditions that would accompany any eventual disbursement.

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:59.040
The bank continues internal talks on whether the package can move ahead under agreed conditions.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:05.960
Stock indexes across Asia rose, led by technology companies, while oil prices declined further.

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:11.760
Reuters attributes the moves to sector-specific trading rather than broad economic data releases.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:16.620
Investors focused on individual company performance within the technology sector.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:22.620
Energy markets showed separate downward movement linked to expectations around global supply levels.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:30.080
Market coverage from Reuters links the gains to continued investor interest in technology firms amid steady demand signals.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:35.120
Energy traders noted separate downward pressure on oil from supply expectations.

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:41.980
The accounts share the observation of divergent sector performance without claiming a single macroeconomic driver.

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:45.160
Trading volumes remain moderate during the session.

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:50.520
Analysts track the movements through standard index calculations across major exchanges.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:55.780
packages. Technology shares lifted indexes while energy prices moved in the opposite direction

00:06:55.780 --> 00:07:00.900
on separate supply signals. Progress worth knowing comes from British police who arrested

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:06.420
two men and halted a plot targeting the Jewish community in Manchester. Authorities described

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:11.980
the action as a successful early intervention. The operation prevented the plan from advancing

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:17.100
beyond the initial stages. Community leaders have acknowledged the role of timely information

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:18.260
in stopping the threat.

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:22.740
BBC reports the arrests prevented the planned operation from proceeding.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:27.900
Community representatives have noted the importance of timely intelligence in such cases.

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:33.180
The accounts converge on the fact of the arrests and the stated intent of the disrupted plan.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:38.000
Police statements emphasized coordination between local and national units.

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:41.720
The case remains under active investigation for additional details.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.300
The arrests stop the plot before it advanced further.

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:50.480
To really understand how international climate and disaster aid reaches local monitoring

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:55.680
systems, consider the layers of agencies, governments, and contractors that decide which

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:56.900
sensors stay active.

00:07:57.480 --> 00:08:03.280
When a donor reduces contributions to programs like those once run through USAID, the first

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:08.360
items often dropped are long-term weather stations and river gauges rather than immediate relief

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:08.900
supplies.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:12.880
Those stations require ongoing contracts and train staff.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:18.700
Historical patterns show that after earlier funding pauses in the early 2010s, several

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:23.320
Himalayan countries lost continuous data series that had previously fed regional flood

00:08:23.320 --> 00:08:25.880
models used by India, Nepal and China.

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:31.140
The process begins with donor pledges that move through multilateral organizations before

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:35.260
reaching national meteorological offices responsible for equipment maintenance.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:40.640
Local technicians then rely on those steady funds to calibrate instruments and transmit

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:45.340
readings to shared regional databases. When the funding chain breaks at any point,

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:50.160
the result is gaps in the data sets that forecast models depend on for accuracy.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:55.200
When reports mention millions more at risk, the concrete check is whether the next

00:08:55.200 --> 00:09:00.740
national budget or donor pledge restores specific line items for gauge maintenance and data sharing

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:05.240
agreements. If you want to go deeper on the Nepal floods and age shortfalls,

